# Legacy URL redirects — Squarespace -> new site
#
# The new site preserves the original permalinks, so most URLs need no
# redirect. These handle the Squarespace-internal paths that crawl tools may
# still have indexed (folder index pages, tags, the empty cart route, etc.).
#
# Format: Netlify/Cloudflare `_redirects` syntax. Vercel users: see
# vercel.json, which mirrors these rules.

# Squarespace folder landing pages -> their first child
/about-1            /aboutthis/            301
/opinions           /future-works-1/       301

# Squarespace blog list pagination
/history/page/*     /history/              301
/books/page/*       /books/                301
/nature/page/*      /nature/               301
/service/page/*     /service/              301
/manufacturers-1/page/*  /manufacturers-1/ 301

# Squarespace category/tag filters
/videos/*/page/*    /videos/               301

# Empty commerce route from the original theme
/cart               /                      301

# Squarespace CMS endpoints that should never be indexed
/config             /                      410
/api/*              /                      410

# Everything else falls through to the 404 page
/*  /404.html  404
